The Gazetteer says the locate level is always Home 3. So you've got 4
levels (.2, .L, .4, .5) for possible Quest bones, assuming 2 is
eligible.

And as Kent said, each special level has its own designation,
irrespective of its depth.

So,
- DoD: .4 to .28 (29 would be castle), plus Oracle, Bigroom and Rogue
= 28
- Gehennom: .2 to .22 (1 is the Valley, 23 and 24 would be sanctum and/
or VS)
plus .V, plus .G (fake tower), plus four demon lairs = 27
- Mines: .1 to .8 (9 would be Mines' End) plus Minetown = 9
- Quest: 4 per class = 52
- Sokoban, Ludios, Vlad's and the Endgame don't leave bones
28 + 27 + 9 + 52 = 116 bones files may exist on one system.

How many bones levels can be loaded in one game:
- DoD can have 29 levels. 1 thru 3 are not eligible, assuming someone
hasn't left wizmode bones. Assume the Mines fork is on 2 or 3.
Medusa and Castle won't load bones, nor will the Quest portal nor the
stairs to Sokoban, leaving 22 bone-worthy levels in the DoD.
- Gehennom can have 24 levels, minus the VS, Sanctum, Wizard portal, 3
Wizard tower levels, and the stairs to Vlad's = 17 levels.
- The Mines have up to 9 levels, minus Mines' End = 8.
- The Quest has 4 bonesable levels.
22 + 17 + 8 + 4 = 51 bones files may load in one game. Not going to
happen, as the odds are around 1 in 3^51, but there it is.



